3. Typed comparison, not string comparison (filemanager.html:486-510).
   The comparator `cmp(a,b,column)` reads `data-` attributes via
   `a.getAttribute('data-'+column)` and coerces per column:
     - name:  localeCompare(..., {sensitivity:'base', numeric:true})
     - rows:  parseInt(av,10) - parseInt(bv,10)
     - size:  parseInt(av,10) - parseInt(bv,10)   // BYTE COUNT, not "25K"
     - enabled: parseInt 0/1 numeric
     - mindate: empty -> Infinity (sorts last ascending, first descending);
               non-empty compared as ISO date string (lexically sortable)
   Verified against a live server: row for big.csv (11442 bytes, renders as
   "11K") carries `data-size="11442"` and small.csv (64 bytes, renders "0K")
   carries `data-size="64"`. The rendered "K" text is never the sort key.
   Empty date range: `data-mindate=""` -> treated as Infinity -> sorts last
   ascending. Confirmed in source lines 500-505.

